1
00:00:21,958 --> 00:00:23,542
I can win!

2
00:00:23,542 --> 00:00:26,792
Against Reiner, I can win!

3
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,042
Hey...

4
00:00:34,042 --> 00:00:35,958
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

5
00:00:35,958 --> 00:00:39,417
Above you! Look out!

6
00:01:58,958 --> 00:02:02,292
Eren!

7
00:03:34,958 --> 00:03:39,958
"The Hunters"

8
00:03:49,375 --> 00:03:53,042
"Trost District"

9
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:02,917
Commander.

10
00:04:03,875 --> 00:04:07,542
Wake up, Commander Pyxis.

11
00:04:07,542 --> 00:04:10,083
You'll get sick if you fall asleep here.

12
00:04:11,083 --> 00:04:13,875
I can't believe you drank all this.

13
00:04:13,875 --> 00:04:16,208
You're not young anymore.

14
00:04:16,208 --> 00:04:20,167
And I'd rather not spend my days
changing your diapers.

15
00:04:20,167 --> 00:04:24,208
Being cared for by a pretty lady
sounds all right to me.

16
00:04:24,208 --> 00:04:26,333
So? What's the situation?

17
00:04:27,958 --> 00:04:33,750
Patrols were sent out once the Titans were
gone from the 1st and 2nd defensive lines,

18
00:04:33,750 --> 00:04:36,958
but any Titan sightings are few and far between.

19
00:04:36,958 --> 00:04:38,458
Hmm...

20
00:04:38,458 --> 00:04:42,583
If Hannes and the advance squad
followed the wall without problem,

21
00:04:42,583 --> 00:04:46,292
they'll be returning any minute now.

22
00:04:46,292 --> 00:04:54,208
It would mean they met the unit from
Krolva District and turned around halfway.

23
00:04:54,208 --> 00:04:58,458
And they couldn't have encountered
many Titans, if any.

24
00:04:58,458 --> 00:05:03,500
If there was a hole in the wall,
it would never work out like that.

25
00:05:06,583 --> 00:05:07,833
Commander Pyxis.

26
00:05:07,833 --> 00:05:09,667
Hmm?

27
00:05:09,667 --> 00:05:12,000
Oh. If it isn't Erwin.

28
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:16,625
I hear you've captured
one of those troublesome mice.

29
00:05:16,625 --> 00:05:17,792
Yes.

30
00:05:17,792 --> 00:05:21,083
Unfortunately, we were one step behind.

31
00:05:21,083 --> 00:05:22,708
Hmm...

32
00:05:22,708 --> 00:05:26,583
But at least it will get those goons
in the interior thinking.

33
00:05:26,583 --> 00:05:32,208
Maybe they'll reconsider how important
their stale beliefs and motives are to them.

34
00:05:32,208 --> 00:05:35,125
Yes, it appears they have.

35
00:05:35,125 --> 00:05:36,875
Look over there.

36
00:05:36,875 --> 00:05:43,083
The Military Police have finally been
forced into an area with Titans.

37
00:05:44,375 --> 00:05:47,750
Can't believe we didn't see any Titans.

38
00:05:47,750 --> 00:05:49,583
Was there really none at all?

39
00:05:49,583 --> 00:05:53,333
Seems so. It's unusually quiet out there.

40
00:05:56,583 --> 00:05:58,917
I wonder if they're still alive...

41
00:05:58,917 --> 00:06:02,042
Can you believe it?
I thought this was an emergency.

42
00:06:02,042 --> 00:06:05,417
Yeah. And everyone's just sitting around here.

43
00:06:05,417 --> 00:06:09,125
Hey, Levi. Where you hiding the Titans at?

44
00:06:10,083 --> 00:06:14,917
Oh? You all seem so disappointed.

45
00:06:14,917 --> 00:06:19,042
Sorry... A shame you couldn't fight Titans today.

46
00:06:19,042 --> 00:06:25,708
If you're looking for another chance,
there's plenty of expeditions outside the walls.

47
00:06:25,708 --> 00:06:30,000
How about we join forces
and face some Titans together?

48
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,500
Uh, well you know...

49
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:34,958
We're busy with work on the interior...

50
00:06:34,958 --> 00:06:37,458
The advance squad's returned!

51
00:06:37,458 --> 00:06:39,500
Inform Commander Pyxis!

52
00:06:42,875 --> 00:06:44,417
I see...

53
00:06:44,417 --> 00:06:47,625
So there was nothing wrong with the wall?

54
00:06:47,625 --> 00:06:48,833
Yes, sir!

55
00:06:49,958 --> 00:06:51,625
As I suspected...

56
00:06:54,125 --> 00:06:57,875
H-However, there's a bit of a situation!

57
00:06:57,875 --> 00:07:00,792
We were heading back to Trost to give our report

58
00:07:00,792 --> 00:07:04,000
when we ran into the Scout unit
led by Section Commander Hange.

59
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Along with them, there were recruits
from the 104th without their equipment.

60
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,833
And it turns out, three of them...

61
00:07:11,833 --> 00:07:13,542
...were Titans!

62
00:07:15,292 --> 00:07:17,458
What are you talking about?

63
00:07:17,458 --> 00:07:20,208
Are you saying there were more?!

64
00:07:20,208 --> 00:07:22,417
Th-Three more of them?!

65
00:07:22,417 --> 00:07:23,708
Who was it?!

66
00:07:23,708 --> 00:07:25,750
U-Uh, well...

67
00:07:25,750 --> 00:07:27,500
Jean, relax.

68
00:07:28,375 --> 00:07:31,042
What happened when their forms were revealed?

69
00:07:31,042 --> 00:07:36,333
The Scouts engaged the Colossal
and Armored Titan in battle.

70
00:07:36,333 --> 00:07:40,333
But by the time we joined up with them to fight...

71
00:07:40,333 --> 00:07:42,000
...it was all over.

72
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:04,208
Unbelievable. What a disaster.

73
00:08:04,208 --> 00:08:07,875
Luckily we were above so we got away unscathed.

74
00:08:07,875 --> 00:08:13,083
Everyone underneath got blasted by steam
and wind. There's nothing they could do.

75
00:08:15,750 --> 00:08:17,708
How's Mikasa doing?

76
00:08:17,708 --> 00:08:22,667
I don't see any bad wounds,
so I'm guessing it's a concussion.

77
00:08:22,667 --> 00:08:24,333
I see...

78
00:08:25,875 --> 00:08:29,083
Armin... You haven't eaten, have you?

79
00:08:29,083 --> 00:08:30,833
I'll get you something.

80
00:08:34,083 --> 00:08:35,958
You've gotta eat.

81
00:08:40,917 --> 00:08:45,917
"Field Rations" "An extremely nutritious ration
utilized by the Scout Regiment."

82
00:08:54,542 --> 00:08:55,833
Mikasa!

83
00:08:59,250 --> 00:09:02,083
Mikasa! It's Eren!

84
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:04,625
What happened to Eren?!

85
00:09:04,625 --> 00:09:06,542
It's those three bullies again.

86
00:09:06,542 --> 00:09:08,792
They took some bread I bought from me.

87
00:09:08,792 --> 00:09:12,125
So he went on his own to get--

88
00:09:12,125 --> 00:09:13,583
I tried to stop him!

89
00:09:15,625 --> 00:09:18,042
Wait!

90
00:09:18,042 --> 00:09:19,875
Give it back!

91
00:09:19,875 --> 00:09:24,292
I thought I told you already.
There's none left 'cause I ate it.

92
00:09:24,292 --> 00:09:25,083
Got it?

93
00:09:25,083 --> 00:09:27,833
That was three days' worth
of food for his family!

94
00:09:27,833 --> 00:09:31,375
You gotta be kidding me. Those table scraps?

95
00:09:31,375 --> 00:09:34,042
Quit it, man. I feel bad now.

96
00:09:34,042 --> 00:09:36,750
If you're fine with vomit, I'll give it back.

97
00:09:40,250 --> 00:09:43,167
Pay him back for what you took!

98
00:09:48,292 --> 00:09:49,958
Hey! Knock it off!

99
00:09:49,958 --> 00:09:50,875
Hey!

100
00:09:50,875 --> 00:09:53,375
You drunk, good-for-nothing soldiers!

101
00:09:53,375 --> 00:09:54,833
Come and break up this fight!

102
00:09:54,833 --> 00:09:56,917
Put a sock in it.

103
00:09:56,917 --> 00:09:59,583
Can't you see the kids are just fooling around?

104
00:09:59,583 --> 00:10:02,750
Like hell they're fooling around!
Come and stop 'em!

105
00:10:04,542 --> 00:10:07,000
It'll be fine, I'm telling ya.

106
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:10,625
Someone will be along
who can help more than we can.

107
00:10:10,625 --> 00:10:11,958
Huh?!

108
00:10:14,208 --> 00:10:16,167
Eren!

109
00:10:16,167 --> 00:10:17,625
Eat this!

110
00:10:26,958 --> 00:10:28,208
It's Mikasa!

111
00:10:29,292 --> 00:10:32,167
Mikasa! Why are you here?!

112
00:10:32,167 --> 00:10:36,958
Eren, if you don't get home and chop wood,
your mother will get angry again.

113
00:10:36,958 --> 00:10:40,000
You little... Don't underestimate me!

114
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:42,583
You asked for it!

115
00:10:42,583 --> 00:10:43,708
Eren!

116
00:10:43,708 --> 00:10:44,958
Let Mikasa handle this!

117
00:10:44,958 --> 00:10:46,583
Yeah, right!

118
00:10:49,708 --> 00:10:51,042
Nice one, Eren!

119
00:10:51,042 --> 00:10:53,292
Don't lose to Mikasa!

120
00:10:55,292 --> 00:10:56,500
The hell you doing?!

121
00:10:56,500 --> 00:10:59,708
I told you to stop the fight,
you damn freeloaders!

122
00:10:59,708 --> 00:11:01,625
What was that?!

123
00:11:01,625 --> 00:11:03,292
Wanna say that again?!

124
00:11:03,292 --> 00:11:06,583
Damn straight I will! You're a waste of taxes!

125
00:11:06,583 --> 00:11:07,667
You son of a--!

126
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:11,458
Don't let it get to you.
It's the truth whether you like it or--

127
00:11:13,625 --> 00:11:14,708
Heh.

128
00:11:16,625 --> 00:11:21,083
That was a pretty good punch
for a chump who runs a stall.

129
00:11:30,750 --> 00:11:33,458
Get 'em! Knock his lights out, Hannes!

130
00:11:33,458 --> 00:11:36,917
You've got this!
Don't let that useless turd beat you!

131
00:11:36,917 --> 00:11:40,542
Hey, you idiots! What the hell are you doing?!

132
00:11:40,542 --> 00:11:41,250
--Cut it out!

133
00:11:41,250 --> 00:11:42,875
--Give it back!
--Cut it out!

134
00:11:48,375 --> 00:11:50,042
Damn it!

135
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:55,708
Knock it off!

136
00:11:55,708 --> 00:12:00,875
Hey! This is turning pretty serious, you guys!

137
00:12:00,875 --> 00:12:02,458
Forget it! Let's scram!

138
00:12:02,458 --> 00:12:03,917
Wait right there!

139
00:12:05,875 --> 00:12:06,750
Wait!

140
00:12:06,750 --> 00:12:09,917
Eren! I don't care about the bread anymore!

141
00:12:09,917 --> 00:12:11,167
Thanks for trying!

142
00:12:11,167 --> 00:12:13,792
Eren. We should get back home, too.

143
00:12:13,792 --> 00:12:15,333
Go home without me!

144
00:12:15,333 --> 00:12:16,167
Eren!

145
00:12:16,167 --> 00:12:18,125
Stop right there!

146
00:12:18,125 --> 00:12:20,500
Eren! Wait!

147
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:26,000
Eren!

148
00:12:46,750 --> 00:12:48,708
Mikasa?

149
00:12:48,708 --> 00:12:50,542
Armin! Where's Eren?!

150
00:12:50,542 --> 00:12:52,750
Mikasa, calm down!

151
00:12:52,750 --> 00:12:54,000
You shouldn't be moving!

152
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:56,625
We don't know how badly you're injured!

153
00:13:06,750 --> 00:13:07,917
Where is he?!

154
00:13:09,125 --> 00:13:11,500
Eren was taken away.

155
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:16,250
Ymir, too, by Bertholdt and Reiner.

156
00:13:19,708 --> 00:13:21,917
Eren, he...

157
00:13:21,917 --> 00:13:24,583
...he lost to the Armored Titan.

158
00:13:25,750 --> 00:13:28,708
It's been five hours since then.

159
00:13:30,250 --> 00:13:32,375
Is anyone...

160
00:13:32,375 --> 00:13:34,667
Is anyone chasing them?

161
00:13:38,792 --> 00:13:39,750
No...

162
00:13:39,750 --> 00:13:41,083
Why not?!

163
00:13:43,667 --> 00:13:47,250
All the horses are on the other side of the wall.

164
00:13:50,208 --> 00:13:56,250
In order to rescue Eren, we have to wait
for lifts to come so we can move the horses.

165
00:13:56,250 --> 00:13:59,417
There's nothing we can do.

166
00:13:59,417 --> 00:14:03,833
Section Commander Hange and
the other officers are too injured to move.

167
00:14:03,833 --> 00:14:09,625
To even send out a small scouting party,
we're going to need more soldiers than this.

168
00:14:09,625 --> 00:14:12,417
Soldiers with experience.

169
00:14:12,417 --> 00:14:13,875
Understand?

170
00:14:21,917 --> 00:14:23,750
Not this again...

171
00:14:23,750 --> 00:14:25,958
Does it hurt somewhere?

172
00:14:25,958 --> 00:14:27,458
No...

173
00:14:27,458 --> 00:14:31,708
I must've hit my head pretty hard, but I'm fine.

174
00:14:31,708 --> 00:14:33,792
But...

175
00:14:33,792 --> 00:14:37,000
When Eren was taken away by Annie...

176
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,375
...I chased them right away.

177
00:14:39,375 --> 00:14:44,125
And fighting alongside
Captain Levi, in the end...

178
00:14:44,125 --> 00:14:47,250
...in the end, we were able to get him back.

179
00:14:51,125 --> 00:14:55,083
But... if it's already been five hours...

180
00:15:06,833 --> 00:15:10,208
Hey, Armin.

181
00:15:10,208 --> 00:15:12,042
Why?

182
00:15:12,042 --> 00:15:16,500
Why does Eren always go
somewhere far away from us?

183
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:20,708
Yeah, now that you mention it...

184
00:15:20,708 --> 00:15:26,875
Eren has always run off on his own,
leaving us behind...

185
00:15:27,875 --> 00:15:34,167
I guess that's just the way things
are meant to happen... for Eren at least.

186
00:15:40,958 --> 00:15:45,333
But all I want... is to be at his side.

187
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:52,583
That's all I ask for...

188
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:07,917
Mikasa? So you're up, huh?

189
00:16:07,917 --> 00:16:10,917
I bet you're hungry. Here, eat this.

190
00:16:12,292 --> 00:16:13,875
Armin, catch.

191
00:16:15,833 --> 00:16:19,917
As usual, field rations are all there is.

192
00:16:23,875 --> 00:16:25,208
Hmm...

193
00:16:25,208 --> 00:16:29,458
Taste neither good nor bad. Same as always.

194
00:16:34,583 --> 00:16:37,625
Speaking of which,
this is the same as always, too.

195
00:16:37,625 --> 00:16:43,958
Ever since the good old days, you two have
been there to clean up the mess of that brat.

196
00:16:43,958 --> 00:16:48,083
That's what I call a lousy relationship. Sheesh.

197
00:16:48,083 --> 00:16:55,292
It's a different time and a different place, but you
kids are doing the same thing you always have.

198
00:16:55,292 --> 00:16:56,708
Am I right?

199
00:16:58,208 --> 00:17:03,667
The neighborhood bullies and Titans
are a little bit different in size.

200
00:17:03,667 --> 00:17:09,125
True... The thing is, that brat isn't
even all that good at fighting.

201
00:17:09,125 --> 00:17:14,250
But no matter if he's up against three or five,
he'll charge in all the same.

202
00:17:14,250 --> 00:17:19,333
By the time Mikasa or soldiers showed up,
he'd been beaten into a pulp every time.

203
00:17:20,625 --> 00:17:22,083
But you know...

204
00:17:23,542 --> 00:17:30,208
I've never seen him win a fight before, but I've
never seen him get beat and give up either.

205
00:17:33,083 --> 00:17:38,417
Sometimes he's so tenacious
that even I think it's scary.

206
00:17:38,417 --> 00:17:42,042
No matter how many times
he's knocked over, he gets back up.

207
00:17:42,042 --> 00:17:43,708
That's the kinda guy he is.

208
00:17:43,708 --> 00:17:47,792
You think he'll get taken away
without putting up a fight?

209
00:17:47,792 --> 00:17:51,833
Nope. He'll keep resisting
as long as he has strength.

210
00:17:51,833 --> 00:17:55,042
Even more so when he's up against just two.

211
00:17:55,042 --> 00:17:58,458
He'll give 'em hell no matter who he's up against.

212
00:17:58,458 --> 00:18:01,167
Until you or I show up to help.

213
00:18:01,167 --> 00:18:03,667
That's how Eren's always been.

214
00:18:10,833 --> 00:18:14,708
I loved those good old days.

215
00:18:14,708 --> 00:18:21,458
If you ask Eren, he'd say those days
were nothing more than a false peace.

216
00:18:21,458 --> 00:18:27,000
But for me, I'm more than happy
to be a drunk, useless soldier.

217
00:18:27,958 --> 00:18:31,875
If it means getting back to
those plain, ordinary days...

218
00:18:31,875 --> 00:18:34,917
...I'll do whatever I have to.

219
00:18:34,917 --> 00:18:37,708
No matter how long it takes to get there.

220
00:18:38,958 --> 00:18:41,000
I'm coming, too.

221
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:46,583
Without you three together again,
I can't bring back the good old days.

222
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,958
They're here!

223
00:19:17,958 --> 00:19:19,250
Hey!

224
00:19:19,250 --> 00:19:20,792
Isn't that...?

225
00:19:22,917 --> 00:19:24,583
Commander Erwin!

226
00:19:24,583 --> 00:19:26,250
And the Military Police!

227
00:19:28,667 --> 00:19:31,667
I never thought they'd ride along the wall.

228
00:19:31,667 --> 00:19:33,917
That's probably the quickest route.

229
00:19:35,417 --> 00:19:37,583
Christa...

230
00:19:37,583 --> 00:19:40,833
I'd prefer if you stayed back, but...

231
00:19:40,833 --> 00:19:43,750
No matter what you say, I won't.

232
00:19:43,750 --> 00:19:47,833
I refuse to wait here when Ymir was taken away.

233
00:19:47,833 --> 00:19:50,292
You two should know how I feel.

234
00:19:50,292 --> 00:19:53,583
Christa has a point, Armin.

235
00:19:53,583 --> 00:19:57,792
We have plenty of reasons
for chasing after them.

236
00:19:57,792 --> 00:20:00,917
One of which I still can't believe...

237
00:20:00,917 --> 00:20:04,708
That Reiner and Bertholdt are our enemies.

238
00:20:04,708 --> 00:20:07,750
I've gotta hear it straight from their mouths.

239
00:20:11,667 --> 00:20:14,917
You made it, Commander Erwin!

240
00:20:14,917 --> 00:20:16,583
Is the situation the same?

241
00:20:16,583 --> 00:20:17,417
Yes, sir!

242
00:20:17,417 --> 00:20:18,667
Good.

243
00:20:18,667 --> 00:20:20,417
Deploy the lifts!

244
00:20:21,750 --> 00:20:23,375
Hange?!

245
00:20:23,375 --> 00:20:24,833
Moblit...

246
00:20:24,833 --> 00:20:27,000
G-Gimme a map.

247
00:20:31,542 --> 00:20:35,375
It might be a long shot,
but there's a giant forest here.

248
00:20:35,375 --> 00:20:37,625
We should head straight for it.

249
00:20:37,625 --> 00:20:42,708
Though, it's not like they have a way
to hide the Armored Titan's footsteps, but...

250
00:20:42,708 --> 00:20:46,042
...I think that's where they're headed.

251
00:20:46,042 --> 00:20:47,708
Why's that?

252
00:20:47,708 --> 00:20:51,625
It's a gamble, but even if they have
the strength to change into Titans,

253
00:20:51,625 --> 00:20:55,917
the other Titans outside
the wall might still be a threat.

254
00:20:55,917 --> 00:20:58,458
Especially after all that fighting.

255
00:20:58,458 --> 00:21:03,583
They might not be as bad off as Eren,
but I'm sure they're exhausted.

256
00:21:03,583 --> 00:21:06,417
Like how Annie was out cold for a while.

257
00:21:06,417 --> 00:21:11,375
Let's assume for now that their destination
is somewhere outside of Wall Maria.

258
00:21:11,375 --> 00:21:14,167
Considering the distance they'll have to cover,

259
00:21:14,167 --> 00:21:18,083
we can assume they'll need
to recover their stamina.

260
00:21:18,083 --> 00:21:23,875
Which means... they'll want to rest somewhere
where Titans are unable to reach them.

261
00:21:23,875 --> 00:21:26,750
At least until nightfall when Titans can't move.

262
00:21:51,625 --> 00:21:53,292
Oh, Eren...

263
00:21:59,083 --> 00:22:00,625
You're awake?

264
00:22:05,167 --> 00:22:06,667
We have until night!

265
00:22:09,917 --> 00:22:15,542
If we reach the forest before nightfall,
we still might make it in time!

266
00:22:15,542 --> 00:22:17,083
Let's move!

267
00:23:58,542 --> 00:24:01,917
Eren wakes up within the giant forest.

268
00:24:01,917 --> 00:24:08,458
Desperate to escape, Eren attempts to
transform once again, but is stopped by Ymir.

269
00:24:08,458 --> 00:24:15,583
Deep in the isolated forest, the emotions
of Eren and Reiner violently clash.

270
00:24:15,583 --> 00:24:18,667
They must settle things once and for all.

271
00:24:18,667 --> 00:24:22,458
Not only for themselves,
but for all those who've died.

272
00:24:22,458 --> 00:24:27,030
Next episode: "Opening."
